   "source": [
    "## Pingouin statistical tests\n",
    "\n",
    "The Pingouin package is designed to make it easier to run various statistical tests, including various kinds of $t$-tests. There are many different ways to use NHST to test various hypotheses, but we will focus on a few common tests that are used in psychology research.\n",
    "\n",
    "one-sample t-test\n",
    ": test whether a distribution has some specific mean\n",
    "\n",
    "two-sample paired t-test\n",
    ": test whether two conditions, measured within subjects, have the same mean\n",
    "\n",
    "one-way repeated-measures ANOVA\n",
    ": test whether two or more conditions, measured within subjects, have the same mean\n",
    "\n",
    "two-way repeated-measures ANOVA\n",
    ": test whether two within-subject factors, each of which may have multiple groups, have the same means"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "editable": true,
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "We will use the `study.csv` file to illustrate these examples."
   ]
  },
  {
